    <node id="NIS">
      <data key="d0">NIS</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">NIS (Network and Information Systems) is a set of regulations established to enhance the overall cybersecurity posture of network and information systems across EU member states.&lt;SEP&gt;The term NIS refers to the directive of the European Union concerning the security of networks and information systems, which serves as the foundation for the national competent authority responsible for this area. NIS is actively involved in cooperation initiatives, particularly in relation to compliance and regulatory measures. In Italy, NIS (National Information Security) is recognized as the national authority overseeing cybersecurity and the protection of critical infrastructure. This authority operates independently and is tasked with ensuring that public administration entities comply with relevant decrees.

NIS plays a crucial role as a liaison for communication and information exchange regarding cybersecurity measures and agreements. Moreover, it is the national competent authority mentioned in the context of digital platforms and information modification. Additionally, NIS is responsible for the registration and communication processes concerning essential and important subjects as stipulated in the applicable decree. Overall, NIS is central to the implementation and oversight of cybersecurity policies and practices within Italy.&lt;SEP&gt;NIS is the national competent authority responsible for the exercise of sanctioning powers according to relevant laws.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f8b069a2848ec3f27bf4ee85e079a65b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-113a7f129467195a5802770e0a180e02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e0e543505f46f01058efe5376e16f1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb94e6dd2cff7234a13092b3648708ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-009b982d5c94c925023f4822a48a235b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5e6f420f6cc4d279f4af29bbcf840e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-484df9d473d54e589fa3c8ffe837ea7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68e0e75c3b7d45965634f03b7bc21efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3574f28f12a3390bb92440df5eda9ca</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_articles/article_21.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_7.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_17.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_22.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_24.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_14.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_38.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_34.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Soggetto">
      <data key="d0">Soggetto</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Soggetto refers to an entity or subject that is mentioned in the regulatory context and can be subject to compliance and penalties.&lt;SEP&gt;Soggetto refers to an unspecified individual or entity that is subject to regulatory measures and compliance requirements.&lt;SEP&gt;Soggetto si riferisce a un'entità o individuo specifico discusso nel contesto di normative o leggi riguardanti la sicurezza.&lt;SEP&gt;Un soggetto è una persona fisica o giuridica riconosciuta dal diritto nazionale che può esercitare diritti e obblighi.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cc2d05ad9613f280438ab5c7cc47980a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9038f356e0f2ad0da2af5d754b346d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ca2f8d685c1e46812789bb56f1f5f7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-009b982d5c94c925023f4822a48a235b</data>
