    <node id="decreto-legge 14 giugno 2021, n. 82">
      <data key="d0">decreto-legge 14 giugno 2021, n. 82</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">The Decreto-legge 14 giugno 2021, n. 82 is a significant legislative act in Italy that establishes comprehensive guidelines and regulations regarding national cybersecurity. This decree-law addresses various aspects of cybersecurity governance, aiming to enhance the country's cybersecurity measures as part of its broader national security framework. It facilitates the implementation of additional policies and provides essential structures for managing cybersecurity effectively. The decreto-legge aligns Italy's cybersecurity measures with the national architecture for cybersecurity, ensuring that procedures and regulations are robust and relevant in addressing contemporary cybersecurity challenges. Overall, the Decreto-legge 14 giugno 2021, n. 82 serves as a pivotal document outlining crucial regulations and provisions that underpin Italy's cybersecurity landscape.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d008e433ea6328598c9f502f5b2a9875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36f036d26b472f0c8e276a34cd467ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ac85b75b9a0982916688ed2e7a5268&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee6efc1b71296d03487494b724c62db6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4afbcc356a5cad070006284b04c6eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b762ae6bc9abced0fc47e1227f90166b</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_articles/article_43.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_4.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_13.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_9.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="legge 4 agosto 2021, n. 109">
      <data key="d0">legge 4 agosto 2021, n. 109</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Legge 4 agosto 2021, n. 109 is a law amending previous cybersecurity regulations to improve governance and effectiveness in handling public administration cybersecurity.&lt;SEP&gt;This law amends earlier legislation related to the government's management of cybersecurity and related policies.&lt;SEP&gt;Legge 4 agosto 2021, n. 109 is a law that modifies the provisions established by decreto-legge n. 82 del 2021.&lt;SEP&gt;The legge 4 agosto 2021, n. 109 is a law that modifies and converts the decrees related to cybersecurity policies in Italy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d008e433ea6328598c9f502f5b2a9875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4afbcc356a5cad070006284b04c6eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36f036d26b472f0c8e276a34cd467ec0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4864bc6c963ba7a38620beb8b978ba44</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_articles/article_15.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_4.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_9.json</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Presidente del Consiglio dei ministri">
      <data key="d0">Presidente del Consiglio dei ministri</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The President of the Council of Ministers is the head of the Italian government, responsible for overseeing the development and execution of decrees and laws.&lt;SEP&gt;The Presidente del Consiglio dei ministri is the head of the government in Italy, responsible for issuing decrees and leading administrative decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Presidente del Consiglio dei ministri, or President of the Council of Ministers, is the head of the government in Italy, responsible for issuing decrees related to national security and administrative matters.&lt;SEP&gt;The Presidente del Consiglio dei ministri is the head of government in Italy and plays a key role in approving cybersecurity strategy proposals.&lt;SEP&gt;The Presidente del Consiglio dei ministri, or the Prime Minister, holds significant powers under the law regarding cybersecurity strategy and its approval.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d008e433ea6328598c9f502f5b2a9875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a799f9bf34f632ba75a0112b5cf13046&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38ac85b75b9a0982916688ed2e7a5268&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4afbcc356a5cad070006284b04c6eff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36f036d26b472f0c8e276a34cd467ec0</data>
      <data key="d4">./cached_articles/article_4.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_40.json&lt;SEP&gt;./cached_articles/article_9.json</data>
    </node>
